# Honor check intent

Never rename a file, change its file extension, or move it just to work around
a rule, verifier, test, eval, or other check when a legitimate fix exists.

- If a verifier, rule, test, or CI check fails, fix the underlying issue.
  Honor the intent of the failing check, not only its glob or filename.
- Do not rename `foo.ts` to `foo.ts.txt`, change an extension, or relocate a
  file so a glob, linter, or `VERIFIERS.md` line no longer matches.
- Users may explicitly override this. Never assume they want a workaround.
- A rename that restores the real extension (for example `.ts.txt`
  back to `.ts`) plus a real fix is allowed.
